# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers (and on the Mac build host) straight from
# a Windows checkout: they must stay LF or bash reads stray \r as part of commands.
# (Defence in depth: build-linux.ps1 also CR-strips scripts before running them, and
# build-app-linux.sh CR-strips the debian text assets it stages.)
*.sh text eol=lf
linux/debian/* text eol=lf
# Dockerfiles too: a CRLF checkout puts \r after the backslash line-continuations
# inside RUN blocks, which silently breaks the docker build.
linux/Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
